# Marketing Campaign Performance Analysis (REVISED VERSION)

## Overview

This project analyses marketing campaign performance using Python, Pandas and Matplotlib.

The aim of the project is to compare different marketing campaigns and identify which perform best based on engagement, conversion efficiency and revenue generated.

The project analyses four marketing channels:

- Facebook
- Instagram
- Google
- Twitter

## Objectives

The main objectives of this analysis are to:

- Analyse marketing campaign performance
- Calculate key marketing performance metrics
- Compare campaign efficiency
- Identify the best-performing campaigns
- Use data visualisations to communicate findings
- Practise applying Python to a real-world business problem

## Technologies Used

- Python
- Pandas
- Matplotlib

## Dataset

The dataset used in this project is a synthetic dataset created for learning purposes.

It contains the following variables:

| Variable | Description |

| Campaign | Marketing platform |
| Spend | Amount spent on the campaign |
| Clicks | Number of clicks generated |
| Conversions | Number of conversions generated |
| Impressions | Number of times advertisements were displayed |
| Revenue | Revenue generated by the campaign |

## Data Analysis

Before analysing the campaign performance, the dataset is inspected for potential data-quality issues, including:

- Missing values
- Duplicate rows
- Negative spending values
- Invalid click values
- Conversions greater than clicks

The data is then used to calculate several marketing performance metrics.

## Key Metrics

### Click-Through Rate (CTR)

CTR measures the percentage of impressions that resulted in clicks.
CTR = Clicks / Impressions
